    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Coats Bend grew in the early 1800s when families such as the Coates and Thorntons settled the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/coats_bend_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1844 Coates/Thornton house, a T‑shaped colonial mansion with a wine cellar, still stands overlooking former farmlands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/coats_bend_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The bend in the Coosa River gave the town its name and made it a natural crossing point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/coats_bend_alabama",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before European settlement, the area that is now Coats Bend was part of Cherokee territory along the Coosa River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/coats_bend_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Coats Bend enjoys a humid subtropical climate, with hot, humid summers and mild winters, averaging 60.7°F annually.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/coats_bend_alabama"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "For over a century, cotton plantations along the Coosa River produced abundant wildlife, fostering a strong hunting tradition among residents.",
